Notebook[{Cell["Exterior Calculus with xTerior", "Title", CellID -> 1100487], 
  Cell["This tutorial develops exterior calculus in xAct, from differential \
forms and Cartan structure equations to Hodge duality, variational \
derivatives, and computations in Schwarzschild coordinates.", "Text", 
   CellID -> 1100488], Cell["Adapted from xTeriorDoc.nb, version 0.9.1, \
updated 19 April 2021, by Alfonso Garc\[IAcute]a-Parrado G\[OAcute]mez-Lobo \
and Leo C. Stein. Copyright 2013-2021, distributed under the GNU General \
Public License. The eight original teaching sections and their mathematical \
examples are retained.", "Text", CellID -> 1100489], 
  Cell["Start with a fresh kernel and evaluate the input cells in order. The \
examples share definitions: section 1 cleans up its geometric objects, and \
sections 2-8 continue in a common session. Some examples deliberately \
demonstrate an error or warning; the surrounding text identifies these cases. \
The settings changed here apply to this kernel session.", "Text", 
   CellID -> 1100490], Cell[TextData[{"Install xAct (including xTensor and \
xCoba) and the xTerior paclet. For individual function syntax, use the ", 
     ButtonBox["xTerior guide", BaseStyle -> "Link", 
      ButtonData -> "paclet:xTerior/guide/xTerior"], "."}], "Text", 
   CellID -> 1100491], 
  Cell["Load the package and suppress the routine definition notices:", 
   "MathCaption", CellID -> 1100492], 
  Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"Needs", "[", "\"xAct`xTerior`\"", "]"}]], "Input", 
   CellID -> 1100493, CellLabel -> "In[4]:="], 
  Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{RowBox[{"$DefInfoQ", "=", "False"}], ";", 
      RowBox[{"$UndefInfoQ", "=", "False"}], ";"}]], "Input", 
   CellID -> 1100494, CellLabel -> "In[5]:="], 
  Cell["In recent Wolfram Language versions, use the package symbol \
xAct`xTerior`Diff for exterior differentiation. Loading xTerior places its \
context on the context path.", "Text", CellID -> 1100495], 
  Cell[CellGroupData[{Cell["1. Example session", "Section", 
      CellID -> 1100001], Cell[TextData[{StyleBox["The user is assumed to be \
familiar with the standard tools of the exterior calculus. The wedge product \
and the exterior derivative only require a differentiable manifold to be \
defined. Other more advanced tools such as the Hodge dual and the \
co-differential require a pseudo-Riemannian metric on the manifold. The \
exterior covariant derivative is built upon a linear connection. In all the \
cases the required structures must be previously defined using commands of \
the packages automatically loaded when loading ", FontWeight -> "Plain"], 
        StyleBox["xTerior`", FontFamily -> "Source Code Pro"], 
        StyleBox[". We refer the user to the documentation of each package \
for a description of the commands used in this session. ", 
         FontWeight -> "Plain"]}], "Text", CellID -> 1100002], 
     Cell["We define a differentiable manifold of symbolic dimension dim and \
introduce some differential forms on it.", "MathCaption", CellID -> 1100003], 
     Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"DefConstantSymbol", "[", 
         RowBox[{"dim", ",", " ", RowBox[{"PrintAs", "->", "\"D\""}]}], 
         "]"}]], "Input", CellID -> 1100004, CellLabel -> "In[6]:="], 
     Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"DefManifold", "[", RowBox[{"M", ",", "dim", ",", 
           RowBox[{"{", RowBox[{"a", ",", "b", ",", "c", ",", "d", ",", "e", 
               ",", "f", ",", "g", ",", "h"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]], "Input", 
      CellID -> 1100005, CellLabel -> "In[7]:="], 
     Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"DefDiffForm", "[", 
         RowBox[{RowBox[{"A0", "[", "]"}], ",", "M", ",", "0", ",", 
           RowBox[{"PrintAs", "->", 
             "\"\!\(\*SuperscriptBox[\(A\), \(0\)]\)\""}]}], "]"}]], "Input", 
      CellID -> 1100006, CellLabel -> "In[8]:="], 
     Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"DefDiffForm", "[", 
         RowBox[{RowBox[{"A1", "[", "]"}], ",", "M", ",", "1", ",", 
           RowBox[{"PrintAs", "->", 
             "\"\!\(\*SuperscriptBox[\(A\), \(1\)]\)\""}]}], "]"}]], "Input", 
      CellID -> 1100007, CellLabel -> "In[9]:="], 
     Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"DefDiffForm", "[", 
         RowBox[{RowBox[{"A2", "[", "]"}], ",", "M", ",", "2", ",", 
           RowBox[{"PrintAs", "->", 
             "\"\!\(\*SuperscriptBox[\(A\), \(2\)]\)\""}]}], "]"}]], "Input", 
      CellID -> 1100008, CellLabel -> "In[10]:="], 
     Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"DefDiffForm", "[", 
         RowBox[{RowBox[{"A3", "[", "]"}], ",", "M", ",", "3", ",", 
           RowBox[{"PrintAs", "->", 
             "\"\!\(\*SuperscriptBox[\(A\), \(3\)]\)\""}]}], "]"}]], "Input", 
      CellID -> 1100009, CellLabel -> "In[11]:="], 
     Cell[TextData[{"The third argument of the command ", 
        StyleBox["DefDiffForm", FontFamily -> "Source Code Pro"], " specifies \
the degree or grade of the defined differential form. Differential forms are \
multiplied by means of the wedge product which is typed in with the key \
combination Esc ^ Esc. This corresponds to the ", StyleBox["Mathematica", 
         FontSlant -> "Italic"], " symbol without built-in meaning ", 
        StyleBox["Wedge", FontFamily -> "Source Code Pro"], ". ", 
        StyleBox["", FontFamily -> "Source Sans Pro"]}], "MathCaption", 
      CellID -> 1100010], Cell[CellGroupData[
       {Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{RowBox[{"A1", "[", "]"}], "\[Wedge]", 
