        Cell[BoxData["0"], "Output", CellLabel -> "Out[149]=", 
         CellID -> 1200107]}, Open]], Cell["This result generalizes to \
exterior powers of the curvature form with any number of factors. Since the \
exterior derivative is zero then there are local potentials for these \
expressions which can be explicitly found in terms of the so-called \
Chern-Simons forms. We can check this result in a number of particular cases. \
Let us define first an index free version of the curvature 2-form and the \
connection 1-form. ", "MathCaption", CellID -> 1100213], 
